"""The single traversability table: every edge type, every node type, and how a path may use them.

This module is the **only** place that says whether an edge type can be walked, in which direction it is
stored, what it weighs and which node types it connects. Everything else derives from it:

* the graph builder stamps ``category``, ``traversal``, ``traversable`` and ``weight`` on every edge;
* ``graph.json`` carries the ``node_types`` / ``edge_types`` registries built by :func:`node_type_entry`
  and :func:`edge_type_entry`;
* ``docs/contracts/traversability-table.md`` is generated by :func:`render_markdown` (a test fails when
  the committed file differs), so the table and its documentation cannot drift;
* the legacy writer renders the old per-domain ``*_relationships.json`` files through the ``legacy_*``
  fields; :data:`LEGACY_EDGE_TYPES` documents what replaced every d13c215 edge name (no code imports d13c215
  analyzer output any more, D-53).

Frozen contract (Wave 0, stream contracts-engine; extended in Wave 3 by I1, DECISIONS.md D-52: the cross-account
sharing types of F-116 and the ``VPC_CONNECTED`` network context of F-105). Change it only through a change request.
Pure standard library; importing it has no side effects.

Regenerate the documentation::

    .venv/bin/python -m aws_enumerator.engine.graph.edge_types --write docs/contracts/traversability-table.md
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import sys
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from typing import Callable, Dict, Iterable, List, Mapping, Optional, Tuple, Union

